        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294-a1">

                <pb facs="0751" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg737"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of State, to Mr. Pierrepont,
                        district attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><seg type="margin">[764]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-08-10"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 10, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acquaint you that the President
                    has decided to place the custody of the gun-boats, seized and held by Marshal
                    Barlow, hereafter with the Navy Department. You will, therefore, so far as you
                        <pb facs="0752" n="738" xml:id="pg738"/> have control over them, deliver the
                    custody of them to such officers of the Navy as shall be authorized to receive
                    them.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards Pierrepont</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States District Attorney, New York.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
